# Backend Standards (Go + Gin)

Layering:

```text
Handler → Business → Repository → Database
     ↓         ↓
   model    entity
```

- Handlers: validate HTTP, map status codes, no business logic. Use `model` DTOs at the edge.
- Business: all domain logic; keep testable with DI. Speak in `entity` types.
- Repositories: database only; no business rules.
- Config: JSON under `configs/` with `${ENV}` interpolation (`appconfig.json`, `database.json`, `api.json`).
- Never hardcode SQL in handlers. Use migrations for schema.
- REST under `/api/v1/...`. Validate every request. Typed responses. Proper status codes.
- Structured logging only — never `fmt.Println` debugging.
- Never swallow errors. Log with context. Return user-friendly messages.
- Secrets via environment variables (injected into JSON config). Never expose tokens to the client.
